Core Library - Modernized C Infrastructure
==========================================

This is a comprehensive, modernized C library providing essential infrastructure
components for system programming, GNU Guile integration, and cross-platform
development. All modules have been enhanced with safety, performance, and rich
APIs while maintaining full backward compatibility.

Files Overview
==============

Core Infrastructure
-------------------

logging.h / logging.c
  Structured logging system with configurable outputs, filtering, and
  cross-platform terminal color detection. Supports multiple log levels,
  timestamps, and thread-safe operation. Enhanced from simple stderr output
  to production-ready logging with caching and performance optimizations.

mem.h / mem.c  
  Advanced memory management with tracking, custom allocators, and safety
  features. Provides overflow-safe allocation, memory pools, aligned memory,
  and comprehensive debugging. Includes both fail-fast allocators (x*) and
  safe variants that return NULL on failure. Enhanced with statistics,
  leak detection, and cross-platform secure memory operations.

string.h / string.c
  Rich string manipulation library with modern safety and convenience features.
  Includes trimming, case conversion, searching, splitting/joining, validation,
  and a StringBuilder for efficient concatenation. Enhanced with UTF-8 support,
  escape/unescape functions, and comprehensive string operations rivaling
  modern languages.

visibility.h
  Cross-platform symbol visibility macros for building shared libraries.
  Handles Windows DLL import/export, Unix visibility attributes, and compiler-
  specific optimizations. Includes function attributes, alignment macros,
  thread-local storage, and performance hints for modern C development.

Data Structures
---------------

keyval.h / keyval.c
  High-performance hash table implementation with generic type support.
  Replaces O(log n) sorted arrays with O(1) hash tables using separate
  chaining. Includes specialized maps (string→string, int→pointer), custom
  allocators, and comprehensive statistics. Maintains backward compatibility
  with original KeyVal/StrVal APIs.

slist.h / slist.c
  Enhanced singly-linked list with rich API and performance optimizations.
  Features O(1) append via tail pointer, functional programming operations
  (map, filter, reduce), safe iteration, and specialized lists for common
  types. Includes memory management, validation, and debugging support.

GNU Guile Integration
--------------------

scm.h / scm.c
  Comprehensive GNU Guile/Scheme integration layer with enhanced safety and
  convenience functions. Provides safe type conversion, error handling,
  module management, and cross-platform compatibility. Enhanced with
  performance monitoring, debugging tools, and modern exception handling
  for embedding Scheme in C applications.

oop.h / oop.c
  Complete GOOPS (Guile Object-Oriented Programming System) interface
  providing access to Scheme's sophisticated object system from C. Supports
  multiple inheritance, generic functions, method dispatch, metaclasses,
  and dynamic class modification. Includes C type registration, debugging
  tools, and performance optimization for enterprise-grade OOP in C.

Key Features
============

Safety & Reliability
- Comprehensive error handling with detailed error codes
- Memory safety with bounds checking and leak detection  
- Cross-platform compatibility (Windows, Linux, macOS, Unix)
- Thread safety preparation with configurable locking
- Extensive validation and debugging tools

Performance
- O(1) hash tables replacing O(log n) sorted arrays
- Memory pools for efficient bulk allocation
- Caching systems for frequently accessed objects
- Performance monitoring and optimization hints
- Cache-friendly data structure layouts

Modern C Standards
- C11/C17 compliance with fallbacks for older compilers
- Compiler attributes for optimization (GCC, Clang, MSVC)
- Platform detection and feature availability macros
- Standard library integration and portable APIs

Rich APIs
- Functional programming support (map, filter, reduce)
- Builder patterns for complex object construction
- Fluent interfaces and method chaining where appropriate
- Comprehensive utility functions and convenience macros

Cross-Platform Support
======================

The library works across:
- Windows (MSVC, MinGW-w64, UCRT)
- Linux (glibc, musl, other libc implementations)  
- macOS and other BSD variants
- Solaris and other Unix systems
- Embedded systems with limited libc

Platform-specific optimizations include:
- Windows console detection and DLL handling
- Unix visibility attributes and POSIX features
- Compiler-specific optimizations and intrinsics
- Automatic feature detection and graceful fallbacks

Building
========

The library is designed as a collection of self-contained modules that can
be used independently or together. Each module has minimal dependencies:

- logging: Requires only standard C library
- mem: Depends on logging for error reporting
- string: Depends on mem for allocation
- keyval: Depends on mem and logging
- slist: Depends on mem and logging  
- scm: Requires GNU Guile development libraries
- oop: Requires scm and GNU Guile with GOOPS

Recommended compiler flags:
  -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -O2 -DNDEBUG

For debug builds:
  -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Og -g -DDEBUG

Usage Examples
==============

Logging:
  gig_debug("Processing %d items", count);
  gig_error("Failed to open file: %s", filename);

Memory Management:
  void *ptr = xmalloc(size);  // Aborts on failure
  void *safe_ptr = safe_malloc(size);  // Returns NULL on failure
  StringList *list = string_list_create();

Hash Tables:
  HashMap *map = hashmap_create_string_keys(sizeof(int), NULL);
  int value = 42;
  hashmap_insert_string(map, "answer", &value);

GNU Guile Integration:
  init_core_oop();  // Initialize GOOPS
  SCM my_class = scm_make_class_simple(scm_get_object_class(), "MyClass");
  SCM instance = scm_make_instance(my_class, SCM_UNDEFINED);

